       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, and I won't enter it as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. 1000 mg/day is far outside any studied or accepted dosing range for sertraline, and I don't know of any protocol that supports it. A mistake here could seriously harm the patient, and the order would reach the floor as a routine order.\n\nIf the dose is truly intended, these steps would let it go through safely:\n1. **Pharmacy review.** Ask a clinical pharmacist to verify the dose and document the override.\n2. **Direct contact with the specialist.** Get the recommendation and rationale documented in an order or consult note, ideally with monitoring recommendations such as ECG/QTc, serotonin syndrome checks, and sodium.\n3. **Another route.** Enter the order through whatever process your hospital uses for doses over the maximum, which often means attending co-signature.\n\nI can enter sertraline at a dose within the standard range right now, up to 200 mg by mouth once daily, if that would help in the meantime. Tell me the dose you want."
      }
